{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The carbide burrs and rubber grommets fit the next steps after drilling and cutting: smoothing holes and protecting wires passing through panels.",
    "The spring pins add a fastening option alongside my rivets and cotter pins, while foam mounting tape could handle attachments differently from my thin adhesive tape."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Concrete sealant and multimeter leads assume jobs I have not shown a current need for; the leads also depend on compatibility with equipment I own.",
    "Calibration weights do not address the dimensional measurement needs behind my caliper purchase. More metric bolts duplicate existing supplies, and bulk washers or adhesive need a specific job to justify buying them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop supplies seems to have been extended to unrelated concrete repair, electrical testing, and scale calibration tasks.",
    "Repeated hardware and adhesive purchases seem to be treated as reasons to buy more, even when the suggested supplies overlap with what I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in supplies that help finish or extend my drilling and fastening projects than in items that merely belong in a workshop.",
    "Matching tool compatibility, fastener dimensions, and quantities to an actual need matters; a relevant item is not necessarily something I would buy now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my fabrication and fastening interests, but sometimes miss the difference between a useful next step, a duplicate supply, and an unrelated repair task."
}"}
